From c340cb16e2d7d612897eba97fd5eec979abbf32f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Fri, 21 Aug 2026 16:46:48 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 09467/11362] [outer-loop] Run receipts: audits must prove they
 ran; QA audit gets a wall-clock budget
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

REQ-CONDUCTOR-RECEIPT-1. Two halves:

Conductor: _run_audit_with_receipt replaces the nine bare
subprocess.run(check=False) audit invocations in research_step's
milestone-close path. The caller now verifies the audit's report file
was (re)written after the call started; the exit code is never the
truth signal. A stale or missing receipt writes a BLOCK line to the
tracked conductor log (journald retention here is hours, not durable).
adversarial_verify --backfill keeps receipt=None (no single report
file) and falls back to the exit code.

QA-layer audit: --budget-seconds (passed as 750, inside the caller's
900s kill timeout). On budget exhaustion it stops, writes a PARTIAL
report naming completed-of-selected, and — the ordering fix — the
rotation offset is now written AFTER the report, advanced by the units
actually reviewed. The old order (state before the LLM loop, report
after ALL units) let the caller's timeout advance coverage accounting
20 units per close while zero coverage happened, silently, since
2026-07-29.

Second concurrent-loss note this session: the codex capstone agent ran
'git restore --worktree' over these files at 16:42Z and deleted the
untracked test file; everything here was re-applied and committed
inside one window.

Takes effect on the conductor's next natural restart.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
